  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "f586048282ed620dcc9666ff8748b96561b52005",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 593727477,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Hi, this is a function that I added and used a few years back (where it was really useful).  Then more recently, I updated the PDCP dissectors (packet-pdcp-lte.c and packet-pdcp-nr.c) to do better error checking with error strings back to UAT, and tried to  add similar checking for the ESP entries here.  I haven't used this function recently (though am hopeful that I will need it again soon).\n\nMy inclination is to commit your change, and I'll add to do my TODO list to review and test it.\n\nI wrote ./tools/check_static.py to look for non-static functions that are never called.  For functions (and variables) that are not mentioned in header files, many were made static or deleted.  For functions that are included in header files, I've mostly left them, but doubt that most of them have ever been called (or will be).  There are currently 240 uncalled functions found in epan/dissectors/",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Martin Mathieson",
